/*
 * SimpletonOS UI - every user-visible string (0.11, 4 Oct 2026).
 *
 * One line per string: STR(ID, "key", "English"). The key is what a language
 * file uses (share/lang/<code>.txt, "key = text"); the English here is the
 * built-in fallback, so a missing or broken file can never blank the screen.
 * share/lang/en.txt is this table written out (simpleton-ui --dump-lang).
 *
 * Rules:
 *   - No user-visible text anywhere else in the code. New text = new line here
 *     plus the same key in en.txt.
 *   - Values are filled in by NAME: "{n}", "{dac}", "{rate}". A translation may
 *     move them or leave one out; it can never crash the UI the way a
 *     misplaced printf "%s" would.
 *   - Not here, on purpose: library text (artist, album, track - never
 *     translated), format names (FLAC, DSD64), button letters, icons, numbers.
 */

